# Git LFS is no longer used by this repository.
#
# The five model files that were tracked by LFS (atomic_lines.csv and the four
# *_p01.h5 weight files) are now stored as normal git blobs: the largest is
# 83 MB, below GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, and the training sets that used
# to exceed it are no longer distributed. Cloning therefore needs no Git LFS
# client and consumes none of the LFS quota.
#
# Old commits still contain LFS pointers; checking one of those out requires
# `git lfs` for the historical files. Current HEAD does not.
